    "title": "Candy",
    "workload": "build 8 ratings arrays of 200000 elements once, alternating narrow (4-value) and wide (100000-value) ranges, then 150 punches of both greedy passes plus the sum. Rating spread is the knob: a narrow range gives long runs of equal ratings where neither greedy rule fires and both passes are pure scans, while a wide range gives frequent strict inequalities so the right-to-left pass does real max-taking work. This kata is the corpus's cleanest exercise of a DESCENDING loop -- the right-to-left pass walks i=n-2 down to 0 with an index-dependent condition -- a distinct bounds-check-elimination surface from the ascending loops elsewhere; every mirror uses an explicit descending index loop rather than a reverse iterator so the loop shape matches. NOTE: the bench passes ratings by reference where the kata takes Vec[i64] by value.",
